Card 3 — PLCO (CA-125 Screening)
Label: The Largest Government Cancer Screening Trial Ever Conducted.

78,209 women. 72 confirmed ovarian cancers. 6 years of annual CA-125.
CA-125 missed 72% of cancers (177/246 never crossed threshold).

What we found:
CA-125 velocity in women who develop cancer: 19.75 U/mL/month
In women who don't: 0.035 U/mL/month
A 500-fold difference — inside a $30 blood test — invisible to snapshot reading.

MUC16 (CA-125 gene) is the 3rd most mutated gene in ovarian cancer. When it mutates, the tumor stops making CA-125. The threshold never fires. The cancer is invisible.

"We analyzed 78,209 women without sequencing a single patient — and proposed the most parsimonious explanation for why a $300M screening program missed 72% of cancers."

Receipt: package-plco-2010.2026-02-27/, scripts/plco/core/config.py

PAGE 3: PLATFORM /platform
Headline: Four engines. One question: will this work for this patient?

Keep it brief. Each engine gets 2 sentences + one number.

Target-Lock — Is the target a real metastasis driver?
38 genes × 8 metastatic steps × 4 biological signals (Evo2 + Enformer + functional + essentiality).
AUROC 0.976 | 11/11 FDA prospective validation

Mechanism Alignment — Are the right patients enrolled?
Cosine similarity between the patient's 8D genomic vector and the trial's mechanism vector.
Identified the LATIFY responding subgroup delta +0.3658 before the trial reported failure

Kill Chain — When does resistance start?
2-of-3 detection machine: CA-125 kinetics + ctDNA/MRD + HRD shift + NRF2 + SLC31A1.
Calibrated against 3,720 patients across 3 published trials via live KELIM API

IO Risk-Benefit Gate — Will checkpoint immunotherapy help or harm?
Net Clinical Benefit model. RULE_OUT verdict for likely non-responders. Mechanistic explanation, not just a score.
AUC 0.822 (LOO-CV, n=29, NeoPembrOV) | SPE TIER_1 subgroup: median OS 25.0 vs 38.3 months (p=0.0038)

